# Node.js/Express + LLM + AI Agents
## Tech Stack
- Runtime: Node.js 20.10+
- Framework: Express 4.19+, TypeScript 5.4+
- LLM: OpenAI GPT-4o, GigaChat, Anthropic Claude
- Agents: LangChain.js 0.2+, LangGraph.js
- Validation: Zod 3.23+
- DB: Prisma 5.12+ + PostgreSQL/Redis
- Auth: JWT + API Keys

## Project Structure
```bash
src/
├── app.ts # Express app + middleware
├── server.ts # HTTP server + clustering
├── controllers/ # Thin Express handlers
│ ├── chat.controller.ts
│ └── agents.controller.ts
├── services/ # Business + LLM logic
│ ├── llm.service.ts
│ ├── agent.service.ts
│ └── prompt.service.ts
├── agents/ # AI Agent definitions
│ ├── registry.ts # Agent registry
│ ├── chat-agent.ts
│ └── research-agent.ts
├── middleware/ # Express middleware
│ ├── auth.middleware.ts
│ ├── rate-limit.middleware.ts
│ └── validate-prompt.middleware.ts
├── prompts/ # Prompt templates
│ └── chat.prompt
├── types/ # TypeScript interfaces
└── utils/ # Helpers
```


## Coding Standards
- Всегда async/await + try/catch
- Controllers → Services → LLM/Agents (thin → fat)
- LLM calls: JSON mode + structured output (Zod)
- Streaming: Server-Sent Events для chat
- Rate limiting: 10 req/min per IP для LLM endpoints
- Logging: structured JSON logs (Pino)
- Errors: custom classes с HTTP codes
